---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What GRWU is, who it is for, and where its data comes from.">
  <div class="prose about">
    <h1>About GRWU</h1>
    <p>
      GRWU is a visual on-ramp to gravitational-wave data analysis. Each article takes one step of
      the analysis pipeline, from reading detector data to measuring a merger, and builds intuition
      for it on real data before handing you the tools researchers use.
    </p>
    <p>
      The articles follow the same path as the{' '}
      <a href="https://gwosc.org/workshops/">Gravitational Wave Open Data Workshop</a>. The goal is
      that a reader who finishes the core track is ready for the workshop's data challenges.
    </p>

    <h2>Three levels of depth</h2>
    <p>
      Every idea starts with intuition: figures you can move and signals you can hear. You can open
      the mathematics behind it, and then the Python code that computes it, without losing your
      place in the article.
    </p>

    <h2>Data</h2>
    <p>
      Strain data and event catalogues come from the{' '}
      <a href="https://gwosc.org/">Gravitational Wave Open Science Center</a>, which publishes data
      from the LIGO, Virgo and KAGRA observatories.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--gutter) 0;
  }
</style>
